config LIB9PFS
	bool "9pfs: 9p filesystem"
	default y
	depends on LIBVFSCORE
	depends on LIBUK9P
	help
		Enable support for the 9P filesystem.
		The following mount options are supported:
		version={"9P2000.u"|"9P2000.L"}
			9P protocol version (case sensitive).
			Defaults to "9P2000.L".
		uname=
			The user name to use.
		aname=
			The file tree to access.

config LIB9PFS_READAHEAD
	int "Read-ahead buffer per file, in KiB (0 disables it)"
	range 0 508
	default 0
	depends on LIB9PFS
	help
		Serve reads smaller than this buffer from a per-file buffer that
		is filled with one 9P read, instead of sending one 9P request per
		read. musl's stdio refills its 1 KiB buffer with a readv() of two
		vectors, so a program parsing a file with fread() otherwise costs
		one or two round trips to the host per KiB. Reads (whole readv()
		calls) of the buffer size or larger bypass it. The maximum, 508,
		is the largest 9P read the virtio-9p transport carries. The
		buffer is dropped on write, truncate and setattr through this
		guest; changes made on the host are not seen while the buffered
		range stays valid (like cache=loose).
